# Era 3, Allocation: places, people, households, fates, self-lies and lore. Year 20, eight winters after era 2:
# the allocation in September, the fever in November, the fire in December. Story lead, 2026-10-23. DRAFT: every
# line in era 3 waits for the author's line approval (ledger row S14). Design: design/eras/era3.md.
# Two classes play it, as in eras 1 and 2: the Inspector line is Pell Furrowe (20), the Militia line Will Brack (44).
# Files: e3_world (this), e3_town (s01 to s05), e3_house (s06 to s12), e3_fever (s13 to s18), e3_witness (Aaron, year 46).
# The era 2 to 3 link is the single go: in q_witness.lwd (q.w.anni.tin goes to e3.start); era 3 ends at e3.end.
# Plates: the q3_* places are areas on their own plates (plates package, 2026-10-22; game/engine/wiring/era3-areas.lwd,
# render/places/q3_*.mjs); the Well House shows a burning plate (q3_well_fire) from e3.well.decide. Props: the new props of
# era3.md section 7 (schoolbook, allocation slip, quarantine chalk, the cut photograph) are painted on the plates; the Tesk
# book is carried as lore and narration.
# Weighted-devices pass, 2026-10-23 (design/device-audit/era3.md): no beat in era 3 turns on paper. The allocation is
# Walter Mott at a board of keys, sending families in or past by sight; the Tarn list is a Tarn man standing at the rail
# and saying it; the fever is chalk, smell and carts; the well talk is a voice in the queue and a hand; Dorrah's book is
# her knot cord. The era's @sense, @load and @echo records are at the end of this file.

