# ---------------------------------------------------------------- the fates, each with its decider
@fate f.e3_flat
pressure: has(e3.allocation)
subject: household e3_sallis
decider: TOBIN
scene: e3.flat.decide, e3.flat.pell, e3.flat.sallis
window: 7
who: Arn
because: the allocation puts ten families to a merchant's house; Tobin Krall says whose hand the far-bank key goes into, the Sallis nine whose bundles are on its floor or Ned Furrowe's son, and their bundles come back over the bridge on the board's cart

@fate f.e3_list
pressure: has(e3.list_offered)
subject: household haldane
decider: ANNI
scene: e3.list.decide, e3.list.signed, e3.list.refused
window: 7
who: Anni
because: Walter Mott gives a far-bank key to anyone a Tarn man will stand beside at the rail and claim aloud; Anni takes the key on Ned Furrowe's word, cuts her thread and puts her bundle on the cart without her father's, or carries it home

@fate f.e3_aaron
pressure: has(e3.aaron_asked)
subject: household haldane
decider: WILL
scene: e3.aaron.decide, e3.aaron.taken, e3.aaron.turned
window: 7
who: Aaron
because: Aaron asks to join the militia on the family's Tarn name; Will Brack holds out the last coat on the hook or turns him away as Hesh

@fate f.e3_bed
pressure: has(e3.fever)
subject: household e3_sallis
decider: CLARA
scene: e3.bed.decide, e3.bed.mim, e3.bed.bet
window: 7
taken: yes
who: Mim
because: typhus in the crowded houses and one bed left on a ward Hollis walks every night asking names and looking at wrists; Dr Clara Lind says who has it, cuts the thread off, and answers for them with a Tarn name

@fate f.e3_sholl
pressure: has(e3.house_over)
subject: household e3_sholl
decider: ANNI
scene: e3.sholl.decide, e3.sholl.named, e3.sholl.split
window: 7
taken: yes
who: Hanne
because: Fenn counts one family too many in the Mott house with his finger; Anni Haldane says the Sholls' name at the rail and Walter moves their key to the hill camp nail, or she says none and her own family's key is moved

@fate f.e3_well
pressure: has(e3.well_claim)
subject: household e3_prayer
decider: GEDGE
scene: e3.well.decide, e3.well.barred, e3.well.opened
window: 7
taken: yes
who: Vesh
because: the poisoned-well talk from the pulpit and a voice in the queue, the gate nailed shut; Constable Gedge keeps the Well House door barred while Fenn's lamp catches, or stands aside

@fate f.e3_tomas
pressure: has(e3.door_barred) & !has(q.tomas_held) | has(e3.door_opened) & !has(q.tomas_held)
subject: household haldane
decider: TOMAS
scene: e3.tomas.decide, e3.tomas.ridge, e3.tomas.stays
window: 7
who: Tomas
because: after the fire, on the runs where nobody held him in the hard winter, Tomas goes over the ridge in the player's man's coat, past the post, to the Tesks' people, or stays and is called Holden at the counter

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- the self-lies (each echoed word for word in Aaron's witness)
@selflie e3.sl.figure
about: GUILT, at the allocation counter, as Tobin Krall praises Ned at the exchange scale in the hard winter, its pan hung in the board room (e3_town.lwd, e3.office.krall)
happened: In the hard winter Ned Furrowe stood at the scale for the office, and the Haldane boy was held at the post and never came home. ? has(q.tomas_held)
happened: In the hard winter Ned Furrowe stood at the scale for the office, and the Hesh on Mill Street went hungry.

@selflie e3.sl.order
about: LOYALTY, on the line at the Well House, with the baton in his hand (e3_fever.lwd, e3.fire)
happened: The Well House burned with the door barred. Mother Vesh and the Varn sisters died inside, and Ilo Haldane at the back window. ? has(e3.door_barred)
happened: The Well House burned. They came out of the door with their clothes alight, and the crowd threw stones at them in the yard. ? has(e3.door_opened)

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- lore
@chain e3.per_af
name: The key and the blank
# both classes meet both: the key slid across the green cloth, and Walter saying aloud whose word left Anni's father blank
route: one-run | e3.lore.slip, e3.lore.per_af

@lore e3.lore.slip
chain: e3.per_af
layer: surface
where: node e3.flat.decide
about: The far-bank key Krall slides across the green cloth: the Sallises' things are on the floor of the flat it opens, and it goes into the hand he chooses.

@lore e3.lore.per_af
chain: e3.per_af
layer: deep
where: node e3.list.read
about: Walter Mott at the rail, twenty years on, saying aloud that his father left Anni's father blank because old Abel Furrowe came down to the counter himself and said, Leave it, Edwin.

@chain e3.margin
name: Who's been, Mott
# both classes hear it from Mott after hours: the boy's visit remembered and said to Holt on the Thursday stairs
route: one-run | e3.lore.register, e3.lore.margin

@lore e3.lore.register
chain: e3.margin
layer: surface
where: node e3.office.oren
about: Walter Mott calling Oren Tesk Haldane aloud at the rail, Haldane, O., husband, and the boys after him, so the queue hears it and it's said, before he takes down an iron key and not a bright one.

@lore e3.lore.margin
chain: e3.margin
layer: deep
where: node e3.margin.walter
about: Walter Mott after hours with the Sallis bottle: his father taught him to remember every caller to an official and say who when asked, and on the Thursday stairs Holt asked, and he said the Haldane boy.

@chain e3.book
name: Dorrah's cord
# the cut photograph at the Haldane room, and the knot cord thrown out of the Well House window
route: one-run | e3.lore.photo_cut, e3.lore.tesk_book

@lore e3.lore.photo_cut
chain: e3.book
layer: surface
where: node e3.list.home
about: The Haldane five, from about year five, in a frame on the room's one shelf: four of them on a bench in the yard, and a clean scissor cut down one side where the fifth was.

@lore e3.lore.tesk_book
chain: e3.book
layer: deep
where: node e3.fire.book
about: Dorrah Tesk's knot cord from the Well House wall, a blue knot for every Hesh child born in the town in forty years and a black one tied over it at each burial, burnt through at the outer coils and blue further in, with Bet's black knot tied last month over the blue one.

@chain e3.carried
name: What was said on the Crown's steps, and in the granary
# the carried words pass one generation: Ned to Pell on the step, Will to Davey in the kitchen; and Walter, who saw
# Will go past the window with the boy, so each class completes it in one run
route: one-run | e3.lore.carry_f, e3.lore.carry_seen
route: one-run | e3.lore.carry_b, e3.lore.carry_seen
route: two-classes | e3.lore.carry_f, e3.lore.carry_b

@lore e3.lore.carry_f
chain: e3.carried
layer: deep
where: node e3.carry.ned
requires: class inspector
about: What Ned tells Pell on the step, word for word as Will said it to him on the Crown's steps in the hard winter, and who said it first.

@lore e3.lore.carry_b
chain: e3.carried
layer: deep
where: node e3.carry.will
requires: class militia
about: What Will tells Davey at the kitchen table, the first time he has said it to anybody but Edie: I carried him. You don't need two for that.

@lore e3.lore.carry_seen
chain: e3.carried
layer: deep
where: node e3.margin.walter
requires: choice has(q.tomas_held)
about: Walter Mott saw Will Brack go past the office window in the hard winter with the Haldane boy on his shoulder, on his own, toward the burial ground, and said so to Holt the Thursday after.

