# ---------------------------------------------------------------- what the player's man carries in era 3 (world/burden.mjs)
@load e3.load.key
name: A far-bank key on a brass tag
weight: 0.2
line: Heavy for its size, and cold. The tag is warm from the man's pocket it came out of.
sense: e3.key_down

@load e3.load.handle
name: The back handle of a handcart with Bet on it
weight: 26
line: The handle comes up and Bet comes up with it, lighter than you'd think, and hot right through the blanket.
sense: e3.cart_wheel

@load e3.load.sacks
name: The Sholls' bed of sacks
weight: 18
line: Damp sacks, five of them stitched into one, heavy as a wet sheep. They smell of the children.

@load e3.load.cord
name: Dorrah's knot cord
weight: 4
line: A rope's weight, still warm. The knots go through your fingers one after another, blue and black.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- the echoes: each fate met later, in the place (world/echo.mjs)
# Every era 3 fate changes a place the story brings the player back to: the Mott house stairs, the hall, the Well House
# yard in the morning, the Furrowe hall stand. Weighted-devices pass, 2026-10-23.
@echo e3.e.sallis_step
place: q3_mott_house
when: has(e3.flat_pell)
tells: fate f.e3_flat
line: The Sallis bundles are stacked on the attic stairs where the board's cart tipped them, tied in sheets, with the far-bank dust still on them. Old Arn steps round them every time he goes up, as if they were somebody else's.
sense: e3.bundle_down

@echo e3.e.sallis_key
place: q3_mott_house
when: has(e3.flat_sallis)
tells: flag e3.flat_sallis
line: Old Arn Sallis has the far-bank key on a bootlace round his neck, outside his shirt, where the whole table can see it. He touches it when he sits down, and when he gets up.
sense: e3.keys

@echo e3.e.anni_wrists
place: q3_mott_house
when: has(e3.list_signed)
tells: fate f.e3_list
line: The shawl bundle is gone from under the shelf, over the bridge on the board's cart. Anni sleeps here still, till the plaster's dry. She keeps her sleeves pulled down over her wrists, and Ilo doesn't look at them.
sense: thread.snap

@echo e3.e.coat
place: q3_mott_house
when: has(e3.aaron_taken)
tells: fate f.e3_aaron
line: A militia coat hangs on the newel post at the bottom of the stairs, too big for anybody in the house but the dead man it was boiled off. The hall smells of the ward because of it.
sense: e3.coat_on

@echo e3.e.boots_grey
place: q3_mott_house
when: has(e3.aaron_turned)
tells: flag e3.aaron_turned
line: Aaron's boots are by the door where Bet keeps them, the ones she blacked for the squad room. They're grey to the laces with cement now, and nobody blacks them.

@echo e3.e.landing
place: q3_mott_house
when: has(e3.bet_dead) & seen(e3.sholl)
tells: fate f.e3_bed
show: absent q.bet
line: The pallet is gone off the landing. The boards where it lay have been scrubbed with lime till they're white, and the whole stair smells of lime, and under it, still, faintly, the sweet smell.
sense: e3.fever_smell

@echo e3.e.back_room
place: q3_mott_house
when: has(e3.sholl_named)
tells: fate f.e3_sholl
show: sound drip 0.2 near
line: The door under the stairs stands open on a bare floor. The sacks are gone. Low on the newel post at the bottom of the stairs there are four small scratches in the varnish where a boy held on.
sense: chair.empty

@echo e3.e.split
place: q3_mott_house
when: has(e3.haldane_split)
tells: flag e3.haldane_split
show: absent q.anni
line: The curtain across the Haldane room is down off its string and folded on the end of the bed, the blue end on top. Nobody has slept behind where it was since the Thursday.
sense: room.cold

@echo e3.e.well_shell
place: q3_well_house
when: has(e3.door_barred)
tells: fate f.e3_well
show: light cold
line: In the morning the Well House is a black box with no roof. The spring still runs out under the doorstep, through the soot, and steams in the frost. The shaft is still through the door handles.
sense: room.burnt

@echo e3.e.ilo_peg
place: q3_mott_house
when: has(e3.ilo_dead)
tells: fate f.e3_well
show: absent q.ilo
line: In the hall the peg by the front door where Ilo hung his hat is bare. Nobody hangs anything on it. The children go round it.
sense: chair.empty

@echo e3.e.ilo_hands
place: q3_mott_house
when: has(e3.door_opened)
tells: flag e3.door_opened
show: person q.ilo still
line: Ilo sits at the end of the door table with his hands in his lap, wrapped in strips of sheet to the wrist. When the pot comes round somebody holds his spoon for him, and he lets them.

@echo e3.e.tomas_coat
place: q3_furrowe_hall
when: has(e3.tomas_ridge)
tells: fate f.e3_tomas
line: Your coat isn't on the hall stand. Your mother has hung your father's old one on your peg instead, and hasn't said anything about it, and won't.
sense: room.cold
